2026-10-28T10:33:23.4163295Z -- v5.3.0 — defrost: duty is measured, the derate is physics
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4163406Z   ok   the inferred estimator reads a real defrost as a PERFECT interval
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4163502Z   ok   an over-1 ratio can no longer park the derate above 1.0
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4163593Z   ok   five defrosting minutes in thirty is a duty of 1/6
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4163665Z   ok   and the interval counts as observed
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4163806Z   ok   a quiet interval is duty zero AND observed — that is real evidence
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4163899Z   ok   an unreadable flag yields duty zero but NOT observed
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4164003Z   ok   a defrost spanning an interval boundary keeps its second half
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4164118Z   ok   a sample stamped before the last does not subtract from the on-time
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4164184Z   ok   zero duty is no derate at all
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4164265Z   ok   the derate is 1 - duty x the loss multiplier
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4164371Z   ok   more duty is always a deeper derate, never a shallower one
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4164475Z   ok   and it is bounded below, so a latched flag cannot zero the pump
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4164559Z   ok   a measured bucket derates from its counted duty
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4164680Z   ok   and a measurement is never averaged with an inference of the same thing
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4164761Z   ok   an untouched bucket still derates nothing
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4164929Z   ok   the summary says which estimator a bucket rests on, and how many defrosts were actually witnessed
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4165031Z   ok   a duty outside [0, 1] is refused, not folded into the bucket
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4165171Z   ok   the range guard rejects only OUTSIDE [0, 1] — 0 and 1 still fold
2026-10-28T10:33:23.4165279Z   ok   a pre-v5.3.0 store loads without raising, and says it was upgraded
